{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Tremble.</b> In the masculine form, like אם תעירו (Song of Songs 2:7), אם תמצאו (Song of Songs 3:8 [8:8]) — in short form." "<b>Be troubled.</b> I have mentioned it. So too the rule of פשוט' [simple forms]. And עורה means to strip off garments; and עורה is from the root of ערום and עריה (Ezekiel 16:7), עריה תעור (Habakkuk 3:9?). And what is correct in my eyes is that they are women, as they sound [i.e. as the words imply]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The Habakkuk citation 'עריה תעור' does not correspond to the standard text of Habakkuk 3:9; rendered hyper-literally as it stands. פשוט׳ appears to abbreviate פשוטות (simple/uncontracted forms)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:22.410196761Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}